    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="0552" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 832.85/55</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-03T18:00:00-03:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 3, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 4, 12.09
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram December 1, 5 p.m. Arrangement applies wholly to commerce
                    between France and Brazil. No provision for utilization of ships in North
                    Atlantic. After France has fulfilled’ the condition of a total of 32 round-trip
                    voyages annually between France and Brazil, the 30 vessels are at her
                    untrammeled disposition.</p>
                <p>Although France represented that her negotiations were conducted for the benefit
                    of the Allies, they will only profit at her pleasure.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
